<title>FRANCE: EU special maize quota covers six states combined.</title>
<headline>EU special maize quota covers six states combined.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A ceiling of 70,000 tonnes on targeted European Union maize exports applies to a group of six countries singled out for special refunds on Thursday, an EU official said, clarifying the latest export package.</p>
<p>The EU set a refund of 20 Ecus per tonne for maize exports to four east European states -- Slovenia, Slovakia, the Czech Republic and Poland.</p>
<p>It also left intact a daily refund of 10 Ecus on maize exports to Switzerland and Liechtenstein.</p>
<p>The official said the maximum quantity of 70,000 tonnes applied to the six countries treated as a group.</p>
</text>
